Point/Click games aren't apparently my favorite type. There aren't so many options like in role-playing games. But  "Chains of Satinav" has a lot of own positive qualities:
- The Dark Eye atmosphere;
- not too bad story;
- good sound, voices, music;
- nice pictures.
On the other hand, characters weren't animated very well. Some puzzles will annoy you.
In generally, the game is worth trying it.

Very good metroidvania-RPG-platformer:
- Length: Good, it took me about 13 hours to 100% everything on Tough difficulty without walkthrough and I didn't rush through it;
- Story: It isn't that good, but the last part is epic;
- Look: It looks nice, the general art style is interesting, but the environments are better designed than the characters;
- Gameplay: Controls are very fluid, combat system is simple yet so much fun (you can also pull off very cool looking combos and feel like a badass once you know how to toy with it).
9/10
***** Please, play with a controller :P

